{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/6/codegen_prompts/7.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed262781723/6`\n- 题号：`7`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed262781723/6/7.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"7\">\n- `description`：沿着每个彩色路径标记指定的方向，在交叉网格线上逐步\"编织\"——交替从网格线上方和下方穿过，每次穿越时改变路径颜色为所穿越网格线的颜色。\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为black。\n  - 网格中有若干条水平和垂直的细线（宽度1像素），颜色各不相同（如red、blue、green等），形成一个稀疏的交叉网格。\n  - 在网格边缘有若干个orange起始标记像素，每个标记位于某条网格线的端点处，且标记旁边有一个方向指示（通过标记与网格线的相对位置确定：标记在线的延伸方向上，表示沿该线向内行进）。\n- `Rule`：\n  - 从每个orange标记出发，沿其所在网格线的方向行进。\n  - 行进过程中每遇到一条交叉的垂直/水平网格线，执行\"编织\"操作：第一次交叉时路径从交叉线\"上方\"通过（路径像素覆盖交叉点，即路径颜色覆盖交叉线颜色），第二次交叉时从\"下方\"通过（交叉线颜色保持，路径在交叉点前后各断开1像素），如此交替。\n  - 每次穿越交叉线后，路径颜色变为该交叉线的颜色，后续段用新颜色绘制。\n  - 路径到达网格边界时停止。\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要同时追踪两个交替状态——上下穿越的交替模式（决定哪个颜色在交叉点可见）和颜色继承规则（路径颜色随最后穿越的线变化）。这两个规则层叠加在一起产生的视觉图案看起来复杂，但底层逻辑是两个独立的简单规则的组合。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/963c33f8, eval/cbebaa4b, eval/332f06d7, eval/247ef758, eval/5961cc34, train/902510d5, train/84551f4c, train/84ba50d3\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"963c33f8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3895\nmechanism=0.4982\nlexical=0.0137\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:path, operation:count, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/963c33f8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop the columns of the top marker downward, stopping blue-ended columns on grey obstacles and letting maroon-ended columns pass to the bottom.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The most numerous non-background color forms stationary grey obstacle pixels.\n- The other two colors form a single 3x3 top-edge marker whose top two rows\n  are maroon and whose bottom row contains maroon or blue control pixels.\n\nRule\n- Erase the top marker.\n- Treat each marker column as a vertical drop retaining its three colors.\n- A column whose bottom control pixel is blue stops immediately above the\n  first grey pixel below that column, or bottom-aligns if none exists.\n- Contiguous maroon-ended columns pass through obstacles and bottom-align;\n  if such a run has a clear down-right slide from a grey ledge, shift the\n  run one column right before bottom-aligning.\n- When a maroon-ended drop lands through a grey bar on the bottom edge, clear\n  the rest of the marker-width gap in that bottom bar.\n\nKey insight\n- The bottom row of the top marker is a control strip: blue cells mean\n  \"stick to the first obstacle,\" while maroon cells mean \"fall through.\"\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"columns of the 3x3 maroon/blue marker on the top edge; the bottom cell of each column is the control pixel\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical drop in each marker column; blue-ended columns stop above the first grey obstacle below, while maroon-ended runs pass through to the bottom with a one-column right slide from a clear grey ledge\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"copy each three-pixel marker column intact; contiguous maroon-ended columns are tested as one run for the slide\",\n  \"dst\": \"settled positions on the same canvas after erasing the top marker\",\n  \"transform\": \"if a maroon-ended drop lands through a grey bar on the bottom edge, clear the rest of the marker-width gap in that bar; leave other grey obstacles fixed\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"cbebaa4b\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2898\nmechanism=0.3625\nlexical=0.0165\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:path, operation:count, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/cbebaa4b.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/cbebaa4b.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAssemble scattered jigsaw sprites around a central yellow anchor by pairing red connector pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = black (0). Several colored sprites scattered on the grid.\n- One anchor sprite contains a 3×3 yellow (4) block.\n- Each sprite has red (2) connector pixels along its edges.\n\nRule:\n- The anchor stays in place; remaining sprites attach one at a time.\n- Each sprite is translated so that one of its red pixels overlaps an unpaired red pixel on the growing assembly.\n- Every red connector must pair with exactly one other, forming a complete joined structure.\n\nKey insight: Red pixels act as jigsaw pegs — each must match exactly one counterpart, and the assembly order is determined by which unpaired connectors remain.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Scattered sprites with red connector pixels are assembled around a central yellow block by matching red connectors to form a connected structure.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"scattered colored sprites with red connector pixels s\",\n  \"dst\": \"attach to the central yellow block or to already-attached sprites d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.red_pixel aligns with d.red_pixel to form connection\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify central yellow block as anchor; Step 2: find sprite with red pixel that can connect to anchor's red pixel; Step 3: attach sprite by aligning red connectors; Step 4: repeat until all sprites connected\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"jigsaw\",\n    \"connector-matching\",\n    \"assembly\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3008\nmechanism=0.3609\nlexical=0.0198\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:marker, object:path, operation:count, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/332f06d7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n\nRule:\n- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n\nKey insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"black square\",\n  \"path\": \"blue pixels \\\"water channel\\\" that is wide enough to pass through until \\\"stuck\\\" because of too narrow\",\n  \"dst\": \"reach same sized red square or \\\"get stuck\\\" on the way where the blue path is too narrow\",\n  \"transform\": \"cover the red square if reaching it\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"247ef758\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3019\nmechanism=0.3816\nlexical=0.0124\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:grid_edge, object:marker, operation:count, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/247ef758.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/247ef758.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n\nRule:\n- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.\n- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.\n\nKey insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"sprite s in the left area whose color appears on the right frame\",\n  \"dst\": \"center at positions d in the right frame\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.color == d.same_row_frame_edges.color and s.color == d.same_col_frame_edges.color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"move sprites from bottom to top, with new covering old\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"5961cc34\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2959\nmechanism=0.3411\nlexical=0.0197\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:path, operation:count, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/5961cc34.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/5961cc34.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nBuild a red ray network by activating blue blobs via directional green ports.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Large blue blobs with adjacent green pixels marking port directions.\n- Start marker: yellow pixel atop a short red segment at grid bottom.\n\nRule:\n- Extend a ray upward from start; on hitting a blue blob, recolor it red.\n- Activated blobs emit thick rays through green ports until boundary or another blob.\n- Cascade until no new blobs are reached.\n\nKey insight: Green pixels encode ray direction and width; the network activates as a chain reaction from one start point.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"port pixels s (start cap pixel; green pixels adjacent to blobs)\",\n  \"dst\": \"extend rays d to activate blobs\",\n  \"path\": \"cast a straight ray from the start port; when a blob is hit, recolor it and emit straight thick rays from its port side through the green pixels; newly hit blobs activate and emit (BFS) until no new hits\",\n  \"transform\": \"activated blob -> red; ray path -> red\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"902510d5\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2664\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
